#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# fourier_sin_series

#% text
# `fourier_sin_series(f, t, k)` gives the Fourier sine series of `f` to order `k`: `b_n sin(n t)` summed for `n` from 1 to `k`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The coefficients are those of `fourier_sin_coefficient` (from the half period `[0, pi]`); `fourier_parameters: [a, b]` scales the frequency by `b`.

#% item
# Lists of variables and orders give the series in products of sines.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
fourier_sin_series(t, t, 3)
#% output
#= -sin(2*t) + (2/3)*sin(3*t) + 2*sin(t)

#% cell
fourier_sin_series(t^3, t, 2)
#% output
#= (3/2 - pi^2)*sin(2*t) + 2*(-6 + pi^2)*sin(t)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `fourier_cos_series`, `fourier_trig_series`, `fourier_sin_coefficient`
